  "id": "COMPOUND:34425 - PROTEIN:3049",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Urs-20-en-3-yl acetate and Cytochrome c4 through a series of molecular targets. The compound is implicated in targeting CDK3/Cyclin E, which is a key component of the G1 phase of the cell cycle and is known to regulate cell proliferation. This target is also a substrate of 1-Hydroxy-3-[4-(3-Methylbut-2-Enoxy)Phenyl]-4-(2-Methylpropyl)Pyrrole-2,5-Dione and 2-(5-Hydroxy-1H-Indol-3-Yl)Acetic Acid, both of which are linked to Cytochrome c4. Additionally, Urs-20-en-3-yl acetate is shown to target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which is a target of Marlignan J, and Marlignan J is also linked to Cytochrome c4. These findings collectively suggest that Urs-20-en-3-yl acetate may exert its biological effects through multiple pathways, ultimately influencing Cytochrome c4. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the regulation of cell cycle-related proteins and their downstream effects on cytochrome c4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
